401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (A notable trend has been observed in the location preferences of game developers in India. Traditionally concentrated in metropolitan areas like Bangalore, Pune, and Hyderabad, there has been a trend of game developers moving away from the metros and non-IT cities towards Tier-2 cities. The newfound flexibility in work arrangements, coupled with advancements in technology that facilitate remote work, has spurred a development boom in cities such as Ahmedabad, Rajkot, Surat, Kochi, and Puri.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
402 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The following are key reasons driving this significant migration:)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
403 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (1. Cost Efficiency)
/E (1. Cost Efficiency)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
404 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Tier-2 cities offer a more affordable operating environment compared to major metros. Lower real estate costs, reduced overhead expenses, and competitive wages make these cities attractive for game development companies seeking cost efficiencies without compromising on quality.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
405 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2. Talent Availability)
/E (2. Talent Availability)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
406 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Sufficient pool of low-skill new graduates from the colleges in tier-2 cities, including software engineers, graphic designers, and animators, who are eager to contribute to the growth of the gaming industry. High investments are made by the game developing companies to get this low skill talent to make them employable. Game developers find it easier to recruit and retain talent in these cities, leveraging the local expertise to drive innovation and creativity.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (3. Large untapped markets)
/E (3. Large untapped markets)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Untapped markets with growing consumer bases for gaming products and services. By establishing a presence in smaller cities, game developers not only benefit from a local market perspective but also expand their reach to diverse demographics and emerging gaming communities that may have been overlooked in metropolitan-centric strategies.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
