418 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Improvements in connectivity, infrastructure, and digital capabilities in Tier-2 cities have made remote collaboration and communication more seamless than ever before. Game developers can now leverage advanced technology and network infrastructure to work efficiently from locations outside of metropolitan areas, facilitating a smooth transition to these emerging hubs.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
419 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (5. Work-Life Balance)
/E (5. Work-Life Balance)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The move to Tier-2 cities allows game developers to enjoy a better work-life balance, with potentially less traffic congestion, pollution, and stress associated with metropolitan living. The relaxed pace of life, access to nature, and community-focused environments in these cities contribute to a more holistic and fulfilling professional experience.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
421 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The migration of game developers to Tier-2 cities in India is driven by an alignment of economic, social, and market factors; this shift underscores the industry's adaptability and resilience in exploring and the potential to overcome challengers to drive creativity and success.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
