/E (Among early-stage startups, a prevalent enthusiasm for seeking investment prospects was observed. 50% of early-stage startups expressed a keen interest in securing investments to fuel their growth, enhance product development, and expand their market reach. These startups, typically at a nascent stage of development, are actively seeking external funding to establish a strong foundation and accelerate their growth trajectory.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Service providers for gaming companies demonstrated an upbeat response to seeking investment prospects. While 50% of service providers expressed an interest in exploring investment opportunities to enhance their service offerings, expand their client base, and invest in technology upgrades, the rest opting for organic growth strategies and reinvesting profits back into the business. This segment appears to weigh the benefits of external investments against the autonomy and control afforded by self-funded growth.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
