482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Early-stage game development companies in India encounter a myriad of challenges that shape their growth trajectory and operational resilience within the dynamic gaming landscape. Among the various hurdles identified, two major challenges emerge prominently: \(i\) business development and \(ii\) barriers to discovery.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (1. Business Development)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 940 0 R
/E (Lack of Industry Connections: New developers frequently lack the industry connections necessary for forging partnerships with publishers and distributors, limiting their growth opportunities.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
485 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 941 0 R
/E (Limited Access to Funding: Early-stage developers often find it difficult to secure capital from venture capitalists or angel investors. Many investors remain hesitant to invest in gaming projects, perceiving them as high-risk ventures with uncertain returns.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
